<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav September inflation 1.2 pct vs 2.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav September inflation 1.2 pct vs 2.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV INFLATION	 SEPT 96     AUG 96     SEPT 95</p>
<p> monthly RPI index rise    + 1.2	+ 2.3	+10.0</p>
<p> yr/yr pct change	    +83.8	+99.2	  N.A.</p>
<p>NOTES -- Figures refer to rump Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>The National Bank of Yugoslavia imposed a stabilisation programme on January 24, 1994, halting hyperinflation of 60 percent per day.</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 2224305</p>
